  "hints": [
    "C strings require a NUL terminator and the `&CStr` type.",
    "`CStr::as_ptr` returns `*const c_char` suitable for FFI."
  ],
  "explanation": "Rust `&str` and `String` are UTF-8 sequences without trailing NUL bytes and return `*const u8` from `as_ptr()`. C functions expect `*const c_char` pointing to NUL-terminated strings, provided by `&CStr::as_ptr()`."
